  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Given that the mean of the following data set is $10,$ find the value of $b:$ \n\n$$\nb,\\,1,\\,b,\\,1,\\,b\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the mean is denoted by $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\n$$\n\nHere, there are $n=5$ data points. Adding up all the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i} & =b+1+b+1+b \\\\  & =2+3b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean is given by the expression\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (2+3b) \\\\  & =\\frac{2+3b}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we're told that $\\overset{\u2015}{x}=10,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =\\frac{2+3b}{5} \\\\ 50 & =2+3b \\\\ 48 & =3b \\\\ b & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
